.TH STAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
stat \- obtain file metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/stat.h>
.PP
.BI "int stat(const char* " path ", struct stat* " buffer ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR stat ()
follows symbolic links and stores information about the NUL\-terminated
.I path
in the writable structure at
.IR buffer .
.PP
.B <sys/stat.h>
declares the Linux x86\-64 kernel's 144\-byte
.B struct stat
layout. Named fields include
.BR st_dev ,
.BR st_ino ,
.BR st_nlink ,
.BR st_mode ,
.BR st_uid ,
.BR st_gid ,
.BR st_rdev ,
.BR st_size ,
.BR st_blksize ,
and
.BR st_blocks .
Time values are provided as seconds and nanoseconds in
.B st_atime
and
.BR st_atime_nsec ,
.B st_mtime
and
.BR st_mtime_nsec ,
and
.B st_ctime
and
.BR st_ctime_nsec .
Other fields are reserved or padding and should not be used by applications.
.PP
Crunch's
.B int
and
.B long
are signed. Interpret fields that represent unsigned kernel values as their
bit patterns. This layout is target\-specific, not a portable C library
.BR "struct stat" .
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero is returned on success.
On failure, \-1 is returned and
.B errno
is set to the positive Linux error number.
Successful calls leave
.B errno
unchanged.
.SH ERRORS
Include
.B <errno.h>
to inspect
.BR errno .
Possible errors include
.BR EACCES ,
.BR EFAULT ,
.BR ELOOP ,
.BR ENOENT ,
and
.BR ENOTDIR .
Other Linux
.BR newfstatat (2)
errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
This Crunch library function is linked from
.BR libcrunch.a .
Its
.B errno
is process\-wide, not thread\-local.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR open (3crunch),
.BR lseek (3crunch),
.BR fstat (3crunch),
.BR stat (2)
